</style><h2>BlinkyBot 0.2.1</h2><ul><li><strong>Kimi Code and Grok are local CLIs.</strong> Pick them with Claude and Codex. BlinkyBot looks up <code>kimi</code> and <code>grok</code> on the login-shell PATH, including <code>~/.kimi-code/bin</code> and <code>~/.grok/bin</code>.</li><li><strong>Sign-in stays on this Mac.</strong> A missing Kimi or Grok login is shown as needing a key. Grok can also use an xAI API key saved in Settings. A key on the Kimi row does not log the Kimi CLI in.</li><li><strong>0.2.0 was the packaged app.</strong> That version restored the BlinkyBot disk image on this OpenBOT tree. This build still has no in-app updater, so install the new disk image.</li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-bot/releases/tag/v0.2.1">Release notes on GitHub</a></p>]]></description>
